message: "If you use this code or these results, please cite the preprint (link to be added when it is posted) and this repository."
title: "A fixed internal signal acts as a relative-position cue: code and results"
abstract: "Three studies in GPT-2 Medium, each frozen before its confirmation run, of a signal cached from the output of twelve attention heads in one indirect-object sentence and added to others: it acts as a cue to the relative position of the repeated name, so name order decides whether it helps or harms."
